<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Strike Trispike out of the two DEATH-SPAWN lists that name it directly.

    A retired seat ruled Trispike removed (cherrypick_inbox.md §A). This patch is the
    half a cherry-pick cannot do, and it is NOT belt-and-braces:

    🔴 CHERRY PICKER NEUTRALISES A PawnKindDef; IT DOES NOT DELETE IT.
    Removing a PawnKindDef sets combatPower = float.MaxValue and clears
    allowInMechClusters / canArriveManhunter / canBeSapper — which is what stops
    the kind being CHOSEN by pawn generation, raids, clusters and manhunter
    packs, because all of those weigh candidates by combatPower.

    ⇒ A DIRECT DEF REFERENCE IS UNAFFECTED. DeathActionWorker_Divide does not
    weigh anything; it reads the list it was given and spawns from it. So a
    cherry-picked Trispike would STILL pour out of every Bulbfreak and Dreadmeld
    that dies. Neither list is a generation path.

    That is the trap this file exists to close, and it generalises: cherry-picking
    a def stops it being SELECTED, never being SUMMONED by name.

    THE TWO LISTS, read from
    Data/Anomaly/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/Races_Fleshbeasts.xml —

      Bulbfreak (kept, renamed Genebulb), :63-70
        deathAction Class="DeathActionProperties_Divide"
        dividePawnCount 4, dividePawnKindOptions { Toughspike, Trispike }
        ⇒ with Trispike gone the list drops to one entry and a Genebulb bursts
          into FOUR Toughspikes. That seat rules it a flavour gain, not a loss:
          one gene-line, one mistake, four copies.

      Dreadmeld (kept, renamed Genemeld), :526-532
        dividePawnKindAdditionalForced { Toughspike, Trispike, Bulbfreak }
        ⚠️ FORCED, not weighted — every entry spawns, every time. There is no
          graceful degradation to rely on here.

    ⭐ AND REMOVING TRISPIKE CLOSES A LEAK RATHER THAN OPENING ONE. Trispike is
    itself a Divide, count 3, spawning Fingerspike — which is being repurposed as
    a tame pet. Keeping Trispike is what would produce a shower of tame Scurriers
    two hops down from a single Genebulb.

    Conditional per list, so this is a clean no-op if Anomaly ever restructures
    these defs, rather than a red error.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Bulbfreak"]/race/deathAction/dividePawnKindOptions/li[text()="Trispike"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Bulbfreak"]/race/deathAction/dividePawnKindOptions/li[text()="Trispike"]</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Dreadmeld"]/race/deathAction/dividePawnKindAdditionalForced/li[text()="Trispike"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Dreadmeld"]/race/deathAction/dividePawnKindAdditionalForced/li[text()="Trispike"]</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
